    "q-69087": {
      "dom_id": "step-q69087",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the value of $(-2)\\sqrt{16}+3.3?$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, we first evaluate the value of the radical, and we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)\\sqrt{16}+3.3 & = \\\\ (-2)\\sqrt{4\\cdot 4}+3.3 & = \\\\ (-2)\\sqrt{{4}^{2}}+3.3 & = \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 4+3.3 & = \\\\ -8+3.3 & = \\\\ -4.7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
