    "q-43669": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43669",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the value of the expression $\\sqrt{{2}^{3}\\times ({3}^{2}-5)÷2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{2}^{3}\\times ({3}^{2}-5)÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{3}\\times (9-5)÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{3}\\times (4)÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{8\\times 4÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{32÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{16} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{4}^{2}} & = \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
