      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$2\\sqrt{({5}^{2}+3)÷2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{({5}^{2}+3)÷2} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{(25+3)÷2} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{28÷2} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
