    "q-69265": {
      "dom_id": "step-q69265",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "What is the value of $2\\sqrt{(3-6)\\times (1-3)}$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?",
      "worked_solution": "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{(3-6)\\times (1-3)} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{(-3)\\times (-2)} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we approximate the value of the radical using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & ≈‭‭‭2.449\\,490\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we approximate the value of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{6} & ≈ \\\\ 2(2.449\\,490) & ≈ \\\\ 4.898\\,98 & ≈ \\\\ 4.899\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
