      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "What is the value of $-0.5\\sqrt{20}$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, we first approximate the value of the radical using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{20}≈‭‭4.472\\,136\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nNow, we approximate the value of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-0.5\\sqrt{20} & ≈ \\\\ -0.5\\times ‭‭4.472\\,136 & ≈ \\\\ -‭2.236\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
