      "dom_id": "step-q69264",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "What is the value of $\\sqrt{2\\times 4-6}$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?",
      "worked_solution": "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2\\times 4-6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{8-6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we approximate the value of $\\sqrt{2}$ using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & ≈‭‭‭1.414\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
